  "name": "Authentication precharge/refund and recovery readiness",
  "changes": {
    "atomic_admission": "Both login budgets reserve together through existing short row-lock transactions; no partial debit and no added advisory locks. Blocked requests stop before credential lookup.",
    "refund_policy": "Successful login resets only its source and refunds one shared-IP charge. Correct password changes reset their budget in the credential transaction. Noncredential failures refund only their provisional charges; failed credentials keep theirs.",
    "transaction_cleanup": "SQL refunds happen before commit; after commit, confirmation only clears memory. Rollback can release the original charge. Refunds match the charged expiry window and are idempotent within the request.",
    "accounts": "Endpoint action and body operation variables are separate.",
    "mail": "Retained detached private jobs with optional mail_php_binary/HOSPITAL_MAIL_PHP_BINARY override; resolved executable, bounded dry CLI probe and explicit readiness reporting.",
    "preflight": "recovery_email.status is unconfigured, ready or unavailable. Configured unavailable delivery fails health. No credentials, jobs, SQL connections or emails are used by the CLI probe."
